@@ -3,6 +3,12 @@
 The web tier drops one raw export per UTC day into data/pageviews/<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv
 at about 01:00 UTC the next morning. This DAG aggregates yesterday's file into
 the `daily_pageviews` table (views and unique visitors per page).
+
+Each run loads the UTC day that its data interval starts on (the run at 03:00 on
+day N+1 loads day N), never "now", so catchup and re-runs of any past day load
+exactly that day. The load is delete-then-insert in one transaction, so re-running
+a day replaces its rows instead of doubling them. `max_active_runs=1` keeps
+catchup to one writer at a time (DuckDB allows a single writer per file).
 """
 
